INF3315 - Privacy Preserving Computation
Sebastian Mai

Layout
  src/task1.py        Task 1: survey API (SurveyAPI) and re-identification
                      risk: k-anonymity of the link with pii.csv, an example
                      attack, and the {County, Age} heatmap
  src/task2.py        Task 2: differentially private API (DiabetesAPI,
                      Laplace mechanism) and the accuracy table: true value
                      vs. MAE of the DP queries at three epsilons
  src/task3.py        Task 3: privacy budget (PrivacyBudget,
                      BudgetedDiabetesAPI), DP age histogram
                      (getAgeHistogram), true vs. DP comparison and bin widths
  src/task4.py        Task 4: Gaussian API (GaussianDiabetesAPI) with an RDP
                      accountant (RDPPrivacyBudget), and total epsilon' of
                      Laplace vs. Gaussian noise against the number of calls
  src/a4_adapter.py   Connects task2.py, task3.py and task4.py to test_a4.py
  src/test_a4.py      Self-check tests for Tasks 2-4 (given)
  src/survey.csv      Survey data
  src/pii.csv         PII data
  report/report.tex   Report source
  report.pdf          Compiled report

Requirements
  Python 3, numpy, pandas, matplotlib, pytest

Running
  cd src
  python task1.py
  python task2.py
  python task3.py
  python task4.py
  pytest test_a4.py -v
